<p>
<b>Features</b>
</p>

<ul class=3D"org-ul">
<li>One-shot and streaming compression/decompression for strings and bigstr=
ings.</li>
<li>Reusable compression and decompression contexts.</li>
<li>Low-level <code>Stream</code> API for manual buffers, and high-level <c=
ode>State</code> API for slice handling.</li>
</ul>

<p>
This is a <b>hard fork</b> of the unmaintained <a href=3D"https://github.co=
m/ygrek/ocaml-zstd">zstd</a> OCaml bindings. It has been <b>fully rewritten=
</b> and is released separately because the original maintainers do not mer=
ge pull requests.=20
</p>

<p>
The main goal of creating this library was to provide a way to incrementall=
y compress and decompress features for my <a href=3D"https://github.com/dx3=
mod/bytream">Bytream</a> library, which is used in my other library, <a hre=
f=3D"https://github.com/dx3mod/rpmfile">Rpmfile</a>, to decode a package=E2=
=80=99s payload as a compressed cpio archive.
</p>

<p>
However, for regular use, you can use the one-shot API.
</p>
